# UCE Phylogenomics Project

## Overview
This project attempted to recover ultraconserved element (UCE) loci from 
published genome assemblies across major chordate lineages using the universal 
Metazoan UCE probe set (Metazoa_Final_red70; Derkarabetian et al. 2025).

## Status
**Closed.** UCE alignments were poorly resolved, possibly reflecting the 
challenges of applying a Metazoa-wide probe set to a chordate-focused dataset. 

The red70 probe set targets 466 loci recovered in at least 70% of the 58 
reference genomes used in probe design. Given that only 466 out of 2,146 
loci met this threshold, it may imply that broadly conserved UCEs across 
Metazoa are relatively limited in number. 

While this filtering was intended to maximize universality across Metazoa, 
it might have come at the cost of excluding loci that are specifically conserved 
within chordate lineages, leaving too few informative sites for reliable 
phylogenetic inference at this scale. 


## Target Taxa
92 genome assemblies spanning five clades:
- Cephalochordata (n=3)
- Urochordata (n=51)
- Cyclostomata (n=15)
- Chondrichthyes (n=13)
- Euteleostomi (n=10)

All assemblies were obtained from NCBI.

## Probe Set
Metazoa_Final_red70 (Derkarabetian et al. 2025, Genome Biology and Evolution)
- 5,098 probes targeting 466 loci

## Directory Structure
- harvest_UCE/   : LASTZ output and sliced FASTA sequences per genome
- Aligned_fasta/ : Multiple sequence alignments per UCE locus
- Unaligned_fasta/ : Raw FASTA sequences per UCE locus
- Tree/          : Phylogenetic tree files
- Scripts/       : Analysis scripts
- 06-summary_table.tsv : UCE recovery summary by target clade


